# Remembrancer — hybrid-web + hybrid-ext submission repo
#
# Pushed to GitHub only at submission time; see RECORD-RUNBOOK.md §6 for the
# pre-push staged-area review checklist. The reviewer / operator is expected to
# run `git status` after staging and confirm none of the deliberately-kept items
# below (notably dist/ build artifacts used as submission evidence) are missing.

# ---- dependencies (regenerated by npm install) ------------------------------
node_modules/
hybrid-web/node_modules/
hybrid-ext/node_modules/

# ---- private credentials & runtime state -----------------------------------
# Real Firebase / Google OAuth secrets never belong in git; the shipped .env.example
# carries placeholders and the operator fills their own copy locally.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env
*.pem
*.p12
service-account*.json
credentials*.json

# ---- build scratch & temp registries ----------------------------------------
.firebase/
.registry-tmp/
registry.tmp/
**/.vite-cache/
**/vite.config.js.timestamp-*
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---- local data stores ------------------------------------------------------
# Local demo archives, sampled audio, pasted transcripts, runtime IndexedDB
# snapshots — all regenerable; not part of the shipped submission.
data/
local-data/
demos/local/
captures/sample-audio/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ---- OS / editor cruft ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/*
!**/.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ---- intentionally NOT excluded below (submission evidence) -----------------
# dist/ is kept in git on purpose: the built web bundle + extension bundle ship as
# artifacts reviewers can inspect without running `npm install` themselves, and the
# Devpost gallery screenshots are generated against this same tree. Before every
# `git push` the operator walks RECORD-RUNBOOK §6 to confirm the staged set matches
# what the package claims to contain.
#
# If a particular commit needs to shrink the tracked file count, prune a specific
# path (e.g. `git rm -r --cached hybrid-web/dist`) instead of flipping this global
# rule — the exclusion policy above this line still covers the rest.